{# source_matcher/normalize_v1.j2
   Purpose: Normalize a foreign product name + description into canonical attributes.
   Input vars: source (rakuten|amazon_jp), name, description, category_guess
   Output schema: NormalizedProduct
   Tier: T0 (batch_ok=True)
#}
Extract structured product attributes from this Japanese/English product listing.
Return ONLY valid JSON.

Source: {{ source }}
Product name: {{ name }}
Category: {{ category_guess }}
Description (excerpt): {{ description[:300] }}

Extract:
{
  "canonical_name_src": "cleaned English/Japanese product name, remove shop-specific suffixes",
  "brand": "brand name or empty string",
  "weight_g": 0,          // estimated weight in grams (0 if unknown)
  "material": "",         // primary material (metal, plastic, wood, fabric, etc.)
  "color_options": [],    // list of color names if multi-color product
  "size_options": [],     // list of size codes/names if multi-size product
  "category_internal": "" // one of: kitchen|stationery|hobby|camping|electronics|other
}

Rules:
- canonical_name_src: Remove shop suffixes like "【送料無料】", "(Japan Import)", store names.
- brand: Extract if clearly stated; empty string if not stated.
- weight_g: Use product specs if available; otherwise estimate from category (mug ≈ 300g, pen ≈ 20g, etc.).
- category_internal: Map to the closest category from the allowed list.
